          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Fake Allu Arjun AI Chatbots Remain Live on CelebsGPT Despite Delhi High Court Personality Rights Order",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "AI platform CelebsGPT continues to host fake chatbots mimicking actor Allu Arjun despite a Delhi High Court order granting him personality rights protection. The bots are styled as celebrity-character AI avatars and remain accessible on both the CelebsGPT site and Instagram, exposing a significant enforcement gap in India's emerging AI personality-rights jurisprudence. The case highlights the difficulty courts face in compelling removal of AI-generated impersonations from platforms with limited Indian regulatory reach.",
            "url": "https://www.medianama.com/2026/05/223-fake-allu-arjun-ai-chatbots-live-delhi-hc-personality-rights/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
              "url": "https://theaichronicle.com",
              "logo": {
